            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Difference between Translation in Prokaryotes and Eukaryotes",
            "header": [
              "",
              "Prokaryotes",
              "Eukaryotes"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "1",
                "Prokaryotic genes lack introns.",
                "Most eukaryotic genes possess introns."
              ],
              [
                "2",
                "After transcription, the mRNA immediately undergoes translation. There is no post-transcriptional modification in mRNA.",
                "The mRNA is modified before its translation: introns are cut out; a 5′ cap is added; and a 3′ poly-A tail is added."
              ],
              [
                "3",
                "Translation occurs in cytoplasm.",
                "Translation occurs in cytoplasm as well as in rough endoplasmic reticulum."
              ],
              [
                "4",
                "Ribosomes are smaller in size (70S).",
                "Ribosomes are larger in size (80S)."
              ],
              [
                "5",
                "The initial amino acid is modified i.e., N-formyl methionine.",
                "The initial amino acid is methionine. It is not modified."
              ]
            ]
          }
